{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And he shall make her drink the waters.</b> To include — that if she said, 'I will not drink' after the scroll was erased, they coerce her and make her drink against her will — unless she said, 'I am defiled' (Sifrei; Sotah 20)." "<b>And her belly shall swell, etc.</b> Even though in the curse he mentioned the thigh first, the waters examine only in the order of their entry into her (ibid. 9)." "<b>And the woman shall be a curse.</b> As I explained — that everything shall be sworn in her." "<b>In the midst of her people.</b> There is a distinction between a person who writhes in a place that is visible and a person who writhes in a place that is not visible."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:38.844640352Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}